---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const email = 'rdm355190@gmail.com';
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="What t-flops is, and who's writing it.">
  <a class="back-link" href="/">← all writing</a>
  <h1 style="margin-top:16px;">About</h1>

  <section class="author-card" data-sketch-frame>
    <div class="monogram" data-sketch-frame="circle" data-sketch-stroke="--accent">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 120 120" role="img" aria-label="A hand-drawn blueprint of a GPU accelerator card">
        <!-- board -->
        <rect x="20" y="34" width="80" height="52" rx="4" fill="none" stroke="var(--ink)" stroke-width="3"/>
        <!-- die -->
        <rect x="40" y="48" width="30" height="24" rx="3" fill="none" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="3"/>
        <circle cx="55" cy="60" r="4" fill="var(--accent2)"/>
        <!-- memory stacks -->
        <rect x="76" y="48" width="8" height="24" fill="none" stroke="var(--ink-soft)" stroke-width="2.4"/>
        <rect x="88" y="48" width="8" height="24" fill="none" stroke="var(--ink-soft)" stroke-width="2.4"/>
        <!-- pcie fingers -->
        <path d="M34 86 V98 M44 86 V98 M54 86 V98 M64 86 V98 M74 86 V98"
              stroke="var(--ink)" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round"/>
        <!-- spark -->
        <path d="M100 30 V38 M96 34 H104" stroke="var(--hot)" stroke-width="2.6" stroke-linecap="round"/>
      </svg>
    </div>
    <div class="author-text">
      <h2 class="author-name">t-flops</h2>
      <p class="author-role">inference · mlops · infrastructure</p>
      <p>
        I kept shipping models and then fighting the part nobody writes down: the serving
        layer. Why the <code>p99</code> spikes on deploy, where the VRAM goes, when to add a
        replica, what a rack actually costs. So I started taking it apart and drawing each
        piece until it made sense.
      </p>
      <p>
        t-flops is that teardown, written in public. The bet is simple: if I can <em>draw</em>
        how inference works at the metal, I actually understand it — and so will you.
      </p>
      <p class="contact">
        Say hi · <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <h2>What this is</h2>
  <p class="lede"><b>t-flops</b> is a hand-drawn field guide to running models in production.</p>
  <p>
    Every post takes one thing the docs gloss over — continuous batching, the KV cache,
    cold-start autoscaling, tail latency, GPU packing — and rebuilds it from first
    principles, with sketches and small animations you can poke at. Less "here's the YAML,"
    more "here's what the GPU is actually doing." Posts are filed by the
    <a href="/layers/">layer of the stack</a> they dig into.
  </p>

  <style>
    .author-card {
      position: relative;
      display: flex;
      gap: 26px;
      align-items: flex-start;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      background: var(--panel);
      border-radius: 12px;
      padding: 24px 24px 20px;
      margin: 1.6em 0 2.4em;
      box-shadow: 0 12px 30px -22px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.55);
    }
    .monogram {
      position: relative;
      flex: none;
      padding: 11px;
      border-radius: 50%;
    }
    .monogram svg {
      width: 150px;
      height: 150px;
      display: block;
      background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 8%, var(--panel));
      border-radius: 50%;
    }
    .author-text { flex: 1 1 260px; min-width: 0; }
    .author-name {
      font-family: var(--font-display);
      font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 6vw, 2.3rem);
      margin: 0 0 4px;
      line-height: 1.1;
    }
    .author-role {
      font-family: var(--font-mono);
      color: var(--accent);
      font-size: .82rem;
      letter-spacing: .08em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      margin: 0 0 12px;
    }
    .author-text p { margin: 0 0 0.9em; }
    .contact {
      font-family: var(--font-mono);
      color: var(--ink-soft);
      font-size: .9rem;
    }
    .contact a { color: var(--accent); text-underline-offset: 3px; word-break: break-all; }

    @media (max-width: 460px) {
      .author-card { justify-content: center; text-align: center; }
      .author-text { text-align: left; }
    }
  </style>
</BaseLayout>
